    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-7387b849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-layout-constrained wp-block-column-is-layout-constrained"><p><strong>International Avian DNA Sample Submission Guide</strong><br>Last Updated: May 8, 2026</p><p>Thank you for choosing Aviantestpro for avian DNA testing services. To ensure accurate laboratory results and smooth international processing, please carefully follow the sample collection and shipping instructions below.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>1. Feather Sample Collection</h2><h3>Recommended Sample Type</h3><p>Freshly plucked feather samples are one of the most commonly used materials for avian DNA testing.</p><h3>Collection Requirements</h3><ul><li>Collect <strong>4–5 freshly plucked feathers</strong> from each bird.</li><li>The feather must contain the <strong>root follicle (quill base)</strong>, as this area contains the DNA material required for testing.</li><li>Do NOT use naturally fallen feathers, old feathers, damaged feathers, or feathers without visible follicle roots.</li><li>Avoid touching the feather root directly with fingers or contaminated tools.</li></ul><h3>Packaging Instructions</h3><ul><li>Place each bird’s feather samples into a <strong>separate clean small plastic bag or sample envelope</strong>.</li><li>Clearly label each sample with:<ul><li>Bird ID or name</li><li>Species (if known)</li><li>Owner reference number (optional)</li></ul></li></ul><p>To reduce sample degradation during storage and transport:</p><ul><li>Before shipping, it is recommended to store feather samples at <strong>2–8°C refrigerated conditions</strong> whenever possible.</li><li>Avoid excessive heat, humidity, and direct sunlight.</li></ul><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>2. Blood DNA Sample Collection</h2><h3>Required Collection Material</h3><p>Blood DNA samples must be collected using:</p><ul><li><strong>Professional DNA blood collection cards</strong></li><li>Specialized DNA sample collection paper designed for molecular testing</li></ul><h3>Important Notice</h3><p>Please do NOT use:</p><ul><li>Tissue paper</li><li>Printing paper</li><li>Toilet paper</li><li>Cotton paper</li><li>Non-professional absorbent materials</li></ul><p>Improper materials may:</p><ul><li>Inhibit DNA extraction</li><li>Damage genetic material</li><li>Cause PCR/qPCR interference</li><li>Lead to invalid or failed testing results</li></ul><p>Using proper DNA collection paper is extremely important for successful laboratory analysis.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>3. Shipping Method and Mailing Address</h2><h3>Shipping Address</h3><p>Please contact our customer support team before shipping samples to obtain the latest sample receiving address and shipping instructions.</p><h3>Recommended Couriers</h3><p>International courier services supported include:</p><ul><li>DHL</li><li>FedEx</li><li>UPS</li><li>EMS</li><li>Other international express services</li></ul><p>For faster international delivery and more stable customs processing, we strongly recommend:</p><ul><li>DHL Express</li><li>FedEx International Priority</li></ul><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>4. Customs Clearance for International Samples</h2><p>International biological sample shipments may require customs clearance procedures depending on the destination country and shipping method.</p><h3>Customs Clearance Fee</h3><p>A customs clearance handling fee applies for international sample processing.</p><ul><li>Standard customs clearance fee: <strong>USD 40 per shipment</strong></li><li>Our forwarding and customs agent currently charges only: <strong>USD 20 support fee</strong></li></ul><h3>Processing Time</h3><p>Customs clearance generally requires:</p><ul><li>Approximately <strong>2–3 business days</strong></li></ul><p>During peak shipping seasons, holidays, or customs inspections, delays may occur and processing time may be extended.</p><p>Please note:</p><ul><li>Customs policies vary by country and courier.</li><li>Delays caused by customs authorities, airlines, weather, or international transport conditions are outside laboratory control.</li></ul><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>5. Laboratory Receiving and Sample Confirmation</h2><p>After customs clearance is completed:</p><ul><li>Samples will be delivered to our laboratory.</li><li>Our laboratory team will:<ul><li>Verify the number of received samples</li><li>Inspect packaging condition</li><li>Take confirmation photos</li><li>Confirm sample information with the customer</li></ul></li></ul><p>Once sample verification is completed and testing payment is confirmed, laboratory analysis will begin.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>6. Testing Turnaround Time</h2><h3>Standard Testing Time</h3><p>For most avian DNA tests, laboratory processing generally requires:</p><ul><li><strong>1–2 business days</strong></li></ul><p>after successful sample receipt and payment confirmation.</p><h3>DNA Fingerprinting Testing</h3><p>Please note that:</p><ul><li>DNA Fingerprinting tests may require longer processing time depending on:<ul><li>Marker analysis complexity</li><li>Sample quantity</li><li>Laboratory workload</li><li>Additional verification procedures</li></ul></li></ul><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>7. Test Reports</h2><p>After testing is completed:</p><ul><li>Customers will receive a <strong>digital PDF laboratory report</strong> by email.</li><li>Reports are typically delivered in electronic format for faster international access.</li></ul><p>Please ensure that your email address is correct when submitting your order.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>8. Sample Quality Recommendations</h2><p>To improve testing success rates, we recommend:</p><ul><li>Using fresh samples whenever possible</li><li>Avoiding contamination between birds</li><li>Individually packaging each bird’s sample</li><li>Clearly labeling all submissions</li><li>Minimizing exposure to moisture and heat</li><li>Shipping samples as soon as possible after collection</li></ul><p>Poor-quality or contaminated samples may affect testing accuracy or require recollection.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>9. International Compliance Notice</h2><p>All submitted samples must comply with:</p><ul><li>Local laws and regulations</li><li>Wildlife and animal transport regulations</li><li>Customs and biosecurity requirements</li><li>Courier shipping policies</li></ul><p>Customers are responsible for ensuring lawful international shipment of biological samples from their country or region.</p><p>Aviantestpro laboratory services are intended exclusively for:</p><ul><li>Avian applications</li><li>Non-human laboratory testing</li><li>Educational and scientific purposes</li></ul><p>No services are intended for human medical or clinical diagnostic use.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>10. Customer Support</h2><p>For shipping instructions, sample preparation assistance, or customs questions, please contact our support team before shipping samples.</p><p></p></div></div><div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-7387b849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-layout-constrained wp-block-column-is-layout-constrained"><figure class="wp-block-image size-large has-custom-border">

